Throughout my journey, my passion for technology, leadership, and social impact has shaped who I am today. At VIT Vellore, I am part of Team Vyadh at SEDS VIT, where I work on the Mars Rover project, focusing on the autonomous subdomain of the software domain. My work here has been instrumental in expanding my knowledge in robotics and IoT, two fields that truly excite me. This passion for technology began during my school years when I built a gesture-controlled robotic arm and a self-balancing robot. These projects not only sharpened my technical skills but also ignited my curiosity about the potential of robotics and IoT.

Beyond my technical endeavours, I am actively engaged in The VIT Anchoring Club, a place that refines my communication, creativity, and teamwork. One of my proudest achievements was participating in the Guinness World Record for the largest Taekwondo display. I’ve also pursued interests in graphic and motion design, blending my technical expertise with creativity. For me, technology is not just a tool but a canvas for innovation.

In addition to that, I’ve always been passionate about creating a positive social impact. One of the most pivotal experiences in my life was delivering a TEDx talk on gender stereotyping. This experience helped me understand the importance of using platforms to speak out on issues that need attention. It fueled my belief in the necessity of challenging gender stereotypes and working towards a more equitable world.

Collaboration and leadership have been a cornerstone of my academic and professional journey. Whether as part of student councils, internships, or cultural exchange programs, I’ve embraced the opportunity to lead with integrity and empathy. It has also allowed me to engage with peers from diverse backgrounds, emphasizing the importance of cultural understanding and global perspectives.

I am constantly seeking opportunities to grow, learn, and contribute. Whether in robotics, design, leadership, or advocacy, I’m committed to blending my technical expertise, creative instincts, and personal values to make a meaningful impact.
